-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",23,{
[705]="70046B20\n1\tMeet with Gurthilm\tJarl Gurthilm can be found in after-battle Osgiliath. You should find the Variag Jarl and learn what he wants.\n2\tTalk to Mablung\tYou should talk to Mablung, who can be found at the Ranger encampment in after-battle Osgiliath.\n3\tCollect supplies (total: 8)\030Gather confiscated treasure (total: 2)\tCollect supplies and payment scattered around the encampment in after-battle Osgiliath.\n4\tBring the payment to Gurthilm\tJarl Gurthilm can be found in after-battle Osgiliath. You should bring the payment to Variag Jarl and make sure he keeps to his promise.\n5\tTalk to Mablung\tYou should talk to Mablung, who can can be found at the Ranger encampment in after-battle Osgiliath.\n",
[706]="7005AF6A\n1\tTalk to Klúso\030Talk to Molkha\tYou should consult Klúso and Molkha.\n2\tTalk to Kyrstig\tKyrstig is waiting to hear what the other scouts have decided.\n3\tMeet the Scout Trio outside Shakhajât\tIt is time to venture inside the fort with your scout allies.\n4\tTalk to Kyrstig\tKyrstig has a plan.\n5\tFind the throne room\tYou should search for the way to the throne room.\n6\tComplete 'Instance: To Ausma's Aid'\tThe throne room awaits you and your allies!\n7\tTalk to Scout-master Ausma\tAusma has been rescued from the clutches of Warlord Dushtalbúk! You should talk to Ausma in Bárgstad.\n",
[707]="700450F8\n1\tFind the meeting location\tFind the meeting location, a tree east of Bâr Nadhron, by the Mouths of the Entwash.\n2\tDefeat the ambushers (total: 4)\030Stand where you were and fight\tYou have been set upon by Variag assailants near the Mouths of the Entwash, east of Bâr Nadhron. Defeat them and do not lead them to the meeting place.\n3\tFind the meeting location\tFind the meeting location, a tree east of Bâr Nadhron by the Mouths of the Entwash.\n4\tDefeat the ambushers (total: 4)\030Stay and defend your allies\tYou have been set upon by more Variag assailants near the Mouths of the Entwash, east of Bâr Nadhron. Defeat them and do not lead them to the meeting place.\n5\tTalk to Togbor\tThe party is under a tree east of Bâr Nadhron by the Mouths of the Entwash. You should hear what Togbor has to say.\n6\tTalk to Gondrad\tThe party has met under a tree east of Bâr Nadhron by the Mouths of the Entwash. You should hear what Gondrad has to say.\n7\tTalk to Togbor\tThe party has met under a tree east of Bâr Nadhron by the Mouths of the Entwash. You should hear what Togbor has to say.\n",
[708]="70071755\n1\tTravel to Sul Madásh\tIrsinith has given you a letter explaining how the rot is consuming Amûma. She has asked that you bring it to a scholar, Orthél, in Sul Madásh.\n2\tSpeak with Orthél\tBring Irsinith's letter to Orthél in Sul Madásh.\n",
[709]="70030143\n1\tExamine a berry-bush\tBerry-bushes can be found near the injured man's camp-site.\n2\tExamine bat-droppings for traces of berries (total: 8)\tBat-droppings can be found near the injured man's camp-site in the centre of Fangorn's eaves. You should examine the bat-droppings to see if bats eat the berries in question.\n3\tCompleted\tThe berries here are certainly not edible, or else the bats would have eaten them.\n",
[710]="7004A38F\n1\tTalk to Overseer Gradrágh\tGradrágh stands with Kurtil and the dwarves on the path above Maudhúl Vôr. Talk to Gradrágh the Overseer and convince him to join the meeting.\n2\tTalk to Kurtil\tKurtil stands by Gradrágh and the dwarves on the path above Maudhúl Vôr. You have talked to Gradrágh and he has given his grudging, conditional agreement. You should talk to Kurtil.\n3\tScout the eastern approach\030Scout the western approach\030Scout the forward tents\030Scout the rear tents\030Scout the meeting spot\030Defeat enemies in Maudhúl Ghûg (total: 10)\tYou should travel to Maudhúl Ghûg, scout it out thoroughly, and thin the Orcs moving about there.\n4\tRaise the Flag\tRaise the flag above the meeting place in Maudhúl Ghûg.\n5\tTalk to Kurtil\tYou should talk to Kurtil in the meeting place at the back of Maudhúl Ghûg.\n",
[711]="7003708C\n1\tTry to help Agelwyn be confident while her husband is away\tAgelwyn needs confidence to lead her people. You should speak with Agelwyn and encourage her to be strong.\n2\tSpeak with Agelwyn\tAgelwyn is in the refugees' hiding spot north of Marton. You should speak with Agelwyn.\n",
[712]="70007317\n1\tBring the bow to Celairant\030Collect the stolen bow\tStarkath can be found outside the walls of Kheledûl. Celairant is at Thrasi's lodge, west of Kheledûl. Celairant told you that his bow was stolen at sword-point by a Dourhand named Starkath and his minions. He has asked you to hunt down Starkath and recover the bow.\n",
[713]="700686AB\n1\tTake a petal from a vibrant flower\030Pluck a clump of fragrant herbs\030Pick a verdant leaf\tGûshida has given you a formula which can help the animals. Find the ingredients across the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl.\n2\tTalk to Gûshida's vendor\tYou have gathered most of the ingredients you need. Now you need fresh water and honey from a vendor that Gûshida recommended. Gûshida's vendor is in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl.\n3\tUse the remedy-making kit\tYou have gathered all you need to create the remedy. Use the remedy-making supplies from your inventory to create the remedy.\n4\tGive the cave-claw in Ezôti's Flat a dose of remedy\030Give the goat in Ezôti's Flat a dose of remedy\030Give the boar in Ezôti's Flat a dose of remedy\030Give the bear in Ezôti's Flat a dose of remedy\tYou have created enough remedy and should give it to the animals in Ezôti's hiding place. Ezôti's hiding place is inside the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl.\n5\tTalk to Gûshida where you first met her in the Upper Ward\tYou have given doses of remedy to each animal, and they all seem better for it. You should report to Gûshida. Gûshida can be found where you first met her in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl.\n",
[714]="7006213B\n1\tTalk to Meriona\tYou have found a necklace on a defeated half-orc in Nímbarth. You should find Meriona outside of Nímbarth and ask her if she recognizes the necklace.\n2\tTalk to Riderch\tMeriona confirmed that the necklace belongs to Riderch. He rests at Stonecrop Encampment, to the south-west of Nímbarth.\n",
[715]="7000E8FA\n1\tCollect Dorwinion White from Rivendell\tDorwinion White can be found in Rivendell, sold by the vintner Sogadan. You should travel to Rivendell to purchase Lendasil's request of Dorwinion White wine.\n2\tBring the Dorwinion White to Lendasil\tLendasil is in the ruins of Edhelion about Thorin's Hall in Ered Luin, far to the west of the Trollshaws. Lendasil has asked you to collect a glass of Dorwinion White for her from the vintner Sogadan in the Rivendell. Once you have the wine, bring it back to her at Refuge of Edhelion.\n",
[716]="70030411\n1\tConstruct barricades along the border of Walstow (total: 8)\tHubryt mentioned that ideal locations for new barricades can be found scattered along the outskirts of Walstow.\n2\tTalk to Hubryt\tHubryt can be found in central Walstow.\n",
[717]="7006278E\n1\tTalk to Taeras\tCalargyl has asked you to bring a report to Taeras of what occurred at Amon Firn. Taeras is at the Scurloc Farm, in north-eastern Cardolan.\n2\tTalk to Edrud\tTaeras has suggested that you speak with Edrud Scurloc. Edrud is at the Scurloc Farm, in north-eastern Cardolan.\n",
[718]="70043054\n1\tSearch for the scouting party at Ost Norhír, south-east of Imloth Melui\tThe scouting party was sent south-east of Imloth Melui, and intended to investigate the old ruin of Ost Norhír. Merenir has asked you to look for the scouting party he sent in search of Orcs, and to bring his men back if that proves possible.\n2\tFree the scout captain from Ost Norhír\tThe scouting party was sent south-east of Imloth Melui, and intended to investigate the old ruin of Ost Norhír. Merenir has asked you to look for the scouting party he sent in search of Orcs, and to bring his men back if that proves possible.\n3\tTalk to Merenir in Imloth Melui\tMerenir is in Imloth Melui, and will want to hear about your encounter with the Orcs in Ost Norhír.\n",
[719]="7000701A\n1\tTalk to Asikko\tAsikko is at the Earth-kin camp, found by skirting the hills northward from the eastern entrance to Esteldín. In order to fulfil his obligation to Trestlebridge, Gondranc has asked you to obtain a book of leatherworking lore promised to him by Asikko, chieftain of the Earth-kin.\n",
[720]="70071B39\n1\tFind Onabóha\tTo make her more amenable to your presence, he suggests you bring her a gift, a treasure stolen from the Ordâkhai at Onabóha, their camp to the south of Jiret-menêsh. You should travel to Onabóha.\n2\tSearch for a worthy gift\tYou have found Onabóha, the Ordâkhai camp near Jiret-menêsh. You should search the camp for treasure.\n3\tTake the Ordâkhai treasure\tYou have spotted a chest filled with treasure inside a tent at Onabóha. You should take the treasure as a gift for Châmelek Gêta.\n4\tTalk to Mêshaget at Jiret-menêsh\tYou have taken a chest fat with treasure from the Ordâkhai at Onabóha. You should return to Jiret-menêsh and show it to Mêshaget.\n5\tWait to be invited inside the halls of Jiret-menêsh\tYou have shown Mêshaget the treasure taken from the Ordâkhai at Onabóha. You should wait to be invited into Châmelek Gêta's halls to meet with her.\n6\tPresent the gift to Châmelek Gêta\tMêshaget wants to introduce you to Châmelek Gêta, the leader of Jiret-menêsh. You should talk to Châmelek Gêta and present her with the gift you brought.\n7\tLeave the Gêta's hall\tYou have met Châmelek Gêta, Lord of Jiret-menêsh and Mêshaget's grandmother. You should exit the Gêta's hall.\n8\tTalk to Mêshaget\tYou have met Châmelek Gêta, Lord of Jiret-menêsh and Mêshaget's grandmother. You should talk to Mêshaget about the encounter.\n",
[721]="7000E5BC\n1\tCollect a coil of rope\030Collect thick furs (total: 15)\030Borrow a sledge from Altti\tThe rope is at a scout's encampment just to the south of Pynti-peldot in Forochel. The sledge needs to be borrowed from Altti the trapper at Jänis-leiri, the Master of the Hunt's encampment by the road to the west. Thick furs can be skinned from any number of beasts in and around Itä-mâ. Kaj has asked for your help obtaining certain items he needs to prepare for his ritual.\n2\tReturn the ritual components to Kaj\tKaj is in Pynti-peldot in Forochel. You have collected the ritual components and should return to Kaj.\n",
[722]="700620E3\n1\tTalk to Rodric\tTangwen has asked you to bring tea to residents of Herne who are taking refuge in the Crossway Inn. Herne is in central Cardolan.\n2\tReturn to Tangwen\tYou should bring the hawkwort flowers and lavender to Tangwen. Tangwen is in Herne in western Cardolan.\n",
[723]="70042C39\n1\tTalk to Bingo on the Last Bridge, east of Ost Guruth\tBingo has decided to reassess his course when you come to the Last Bridge, on the border between the Lone-lands and the Trollshaws.\n2\tTalk to Bingo on the Last Bridge and find a good place to make camp\tBingo's legs are sore from the walk from Ost Guruth, and wants to find a good place to stop for the night. He said to speak with him on the Last Bridge when you are ready to look for a good place to make camp.\n3\tTalk to Bingo in the Trollshaws, east of the Last Bridge, north of the road\tBingo is north of the road, a short distance east of the Last Bridge, in the Trollshaws. Bingo had a restful night, but you did not.\n",
[724]="7006C6F5\n1\tSpeak with Lathagwid at Shonith and describe what you saw\tRaphûz and Ashâmi intend to leave Urmâkh to return to Lathagwid. They ask that you go to Shonith to share your description with Lathagwid. She may know the foe you witnessed. Lathagwid can be found near the oasis in Shonith.\n2\tSpeak with Ashâmi in the oasis of Shonith\tLathagwid could not recall a foe in all her long life. She told Ashâmi and Raphûz there is a dead land north of Imhûlar but could recall nothing more. Seek out Ashâmi in Shonith to speak with her about Lathagwid's response.\n3\tSpeak with Raphûz in the oasis of Shonith\tAshâmi is frightened and inspired by what she heard and what you have seen. She asked for time to think apart from Raphûz and determine the path she wishes to follow. She hopes Raphûz feels the same. Seek Raphûz in Shonith.\n",
[725]="7002EFEF\n1\tFind Rodwen's sword\tWilferth is at the Rohirrim-camp in the East Wall. You remember returning a high-quality blade of Gondorian make to Wilferth from the Orc that possessed it. Perhaps this was Rodwen's blade.\n2\tBring the sword to Rodwen\tRodwen is at Hestil's camp, near Parth Galen in the East Wall. You have recovered Rodwen's sword and should bring it to her.\n",
[726]="70019A72\n1\tDrunken revellers admonished (total: 5)\tDuring the evening hours, find revellers in Imlad Lalaith who have indulged overmuch in wine and have become too loud or boisterous and remind them of their manners. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tSpeak with Maliriel at Imlad Lalaith\tYou should speak with Maliriel at Imlad Lalaith.\n",
[727]="70022C1D\n1\tUse the hint inside the Haunted Burrow to determine which bottle to drink from (this will help you navigate the course)\tThe bottles can be found at the entrance to the Haunted Burrow. You should use the correct bottle to navigate to the entrance to the Creeping Wing -- but be wary of which bottle you drink from!\n2\tGet to the door of the Cobwebbed Wing\tThe entrance to the Cobwebbed Wing is at the other end of the Main Cellar. You must make it to the entrance to the Cobwebbed Wing before the time runs out.\n3\tUse the clue to determine which bottle to choose\tThe potion bottles that will enable you to move through the Cobwebbed Wing are at the entrance to the wing. You should examine the clue and select the correct bottle.\n4\tGo to the entrance to the Creeping Wing\tThe door to the Creeping Wing is somewhere in the Cobwebbed Wing. You should get to the door of the Creeping Wing before the time expires.\n5\tDetermine which bottle you should choose\tThe bottles can be found at the entrance to the Creeping Wing in the Haunted Burrow. You should use the correct bottle to navigate to the exit of the Creeping Wing -- but be wary of which bottle you drink from!\n6\tFind the door to the Basement\tThe door to the basement is the exit to the Creeping Wing. You should seek the exit to the Creeping Wing before the time runs out.\n7\tRead the clue to determine which bottle to use\tThe bottles can be found at the entrance to the Basement in the Haunted Burrow. You should use the correct bottle to navigate to the exit of the Basement -- but be wary of which bottle you drink from!\n8\tFind the door out of the basement\tThe door to the Main Cellar is at the other end of the basement. You should return to the Main Cellar as quickly as you can.\n9\tReturn to the main entrance of the Haunted Burrow\tThe exit to the Party Tree is the door that let you into the Haunted Burrow. You should find your way back to the Main Entrance.\n10\tTalk to Adalgrim Goodbody outisde the Haunted Burrow\tAdalgrim Goodbody stands outside the Haunted Burrow, near the Party Tree. You should return to Adalgrim Goodbody with news of your success at the riddle-game.\n",
[728]="700136FF\n1\tSolve Twisttongue's Riddle\tYou should try and solve Falgeirr Twisttongue's riddle: I can sizzle like bacon; I am made with an egg, I have plenty of backbone, but lack a good leg, I peel layers like onions, but still remain whole, I can be long, like a flag-pole, yet fit in small holes. What am I? The solution to the riddle can be found somewhere in the Silvertine Lodes.\n",
[729]="700375C2\n1\tBring Thane Ordlac's token to Thane Torferth\tThane Torferth is at Tordag's encampment, north-west of Stoke. Lúfa bade you seek out the aid of young Thane Torferth of Torsbury.\n",
[730]="7004A8FB\n1\tClear debris from Cirith Ungol (total: 14)\tDebris can be found throughout Cirith Ungol. Danghát has asked you to help clear debris from Cirith Ungol.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have cleared a great deal of debris from Cirith Ungol.\n",
[731]="70007042\n1\tCollect stolen crates (total: 8)\030Defeat half-orcs (total: 10)\tNaerost lies just east of Amon Sûl, north of Hunulf Munce. Hunulf Munce has asked you to seek out and slay the hirelings who guard the relics packed for shipment and return as many of the relics as you can to the Eglain.\n2\tBring the stolen crates to Hunulf Munce\tHunulf awaits your return at the east edge of Minas Eriol, near the bridge over the gorge. You should return with the recovered relics to Hunulf Munce.\n",
[732]="7001AF93\n1\tCryptic as it may be, it appears the shade is looking for something. Perhaps you can search the many barrows throughout the north Barrow-downs for clues.\t\n2\tThe Wandering Shade's barrow is in the northern Barrow-downs. Your investigation lead you to a barrow where the earth was recently disturbed by the movement of the heavy, stone door to the grave within the mound. You should search the barrow, for signs that link the shade to this location.\t\n3\tDeliver the ring to the Wandering Shade in the Barrow-downs\tThe Wandering Shade roams the northern Barrow-downs. You have found the Wandering Shade's ring and should now return it to its owner.\n",
[733]="70028E1B\n1\tMine for ore at towering rocks (total: 6)\tOre deposits can be found along towering rocks in Pren Gwydh just south of Rook's Hut. You should collect ore deposits for the smithing of the ring Rook desires.\n2\tForge a ring that will satisfy Rook\tThere is a small forge at Rook's Hut in Pren Gwydh. You should return to the hut with the ore you collected and craft a sufficient ring.\n3\tBring the ordinary ring to Rook at his hut\tRook is at his hut in Pren Gwydh, waiting for a Ring of Power to be brought to him. You should bring Rook the ring you forged from local metal veins and see if it will suffice for his needs.\n",
[734]="7001078A\n1\tCatch as many fish as you can in twenty minutes\tFish can be caught in the river running through Thorin's Hall. Láfi has given you some time to catch fish for the Lithe Festival.\n",
[735]="7000C053\n1\tSeek the white marker stone indicating the path to Tâl Bruinen\tEchad Candelleth sits atop a hill in Tâl Bruinen, south-east of Thorenhad. Elrohir told you to head east along the main road to the Bruinen, where you will find another white marker stone. Elrohir told you to go to Echad Candelleth and aid Candelleth's company, while he and Elladan inform their father of the threats you discovered in Nan Tornaeth.\n2\tTalk to an Elf-scout in Tâl Bruinen\tEchad Candelleth sits atop a hill in Tâl Bruinen, south-east of Thorenhad. Elrohir told you to take dirt path south as it climbs the hills above the western bank of the river. He advised that you to pay close attention to the path, as it is covered in brush and crossed by streams, but said that you might find a scout somewhere along its length to guide you to the encampment. Elrohir has asked you to help the Elves at Echad Candelleth with their charge of keeping Tâl Bruinen free from danger.\n3\tTalk to Nestael\tNestael is at Echad Candelleth, the Elf-camp in Tâl Bruinen, just over the south-east hill from Haradir's post. Haradir told you to introduce yourself to Nestael at Echad Candelleth, and she would let you know what aid you might lend.\n",
[736]="7006B718\n1\tReach Ub Nishir to the north of Maurûsh\tReach Ub Nishir, the camp to the north of Maurûsh and speak with Galâmka\n2\tSpeak with Galâmka\tSpeak with Galâmka in Ub Nishir.\n",
})
